Harmonia evaluation harness - dataset credits and licensing
===========================================================

The harness downloads third-party datasets at runtime into eval/datasets/
(gitignored). None of that data is vendored or redistributed in this
repository. The licenses below cover only the downloaded data on your disk,
never anything committed here. Harmonia's own code is under the repository's
license.


GiantSteps+ EDM Key dataset  (key evaluation)
---------------------------------------------
600 two-minute electronic-music excerpts with corrected key annotations.
Source:   Zenodo record 1095691  (https://zenodo.org/record/1095691)
License:  Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
Citation: Knees, P., Faraldo, A., Herrera, P., Vogl, R., Boeck, S.,
          Hoerschlaeger, F., Le Goff, M. (2015). Two data sets for tempo
          estimation and key detection in electronic dance music annotated
          from user corrections. ISMIR 2015.

Note: this is the re-annotated GiantSteps+ set (600 tracks), NOT the original
GiantSteps key set (604 tracks). See README.md - scores are not directly
comparable to papers that use the original 604-track set.


GTZAN Genre Collection  (tempo evaluation - audio)
--------------------------------------------------
1000 thirty-second excerpts across 10 genres.
Source:   public mirror on Hugging Face (marsyas/gtzan). The original marsyas
          source (opihi.cs.uvic.ca) is no longer available.
License:  no clear license is stated for the GTZAN audio. It is fetched at
          runtime and NOT redistributed here.
Citation: Tzanetakis, G., & Cook, P. (2002). Musical genre classification of
          audio signals. IEEE Transactions on Speech and Audio Processing,
          10(5), 293-302.


GTZAN tempo annotations  (tempo evaluation - ground truth)
----------------------------------------------------------
One tempo value (BPM) per track.
Source:   TempoBeatDownbeat / gtzan_tempo_beat (GitHub), as indexed by
          mirdata's gtzan_genre loader.
License:  no license is stated for these tempo annotations. They are fetched
          at runtime and NOT redistributed here.


Tooling
-------
Dataset download and loading use mirdata (BSD-3-Clause). Key scoring is
cross-checked against mir_eval (MIT). Neither is vendored; both are listed in
eval/requirements.txt.
